more

https://orchestraltools.example/link/7954675825a51e5c

https://orchestraltools.example/link/ddb67abd409d8a4e

https://orchestraltools.example/link/ddb67abd409d8a4e

UPDATE AVAILABLE
https://orchestraltools.example/link/ddb67abd409d8a4e

SINEplayer version 1.4.0 is out and available to download now. It=E2=80=99s a=
 major update that includes some frequently requested features:

New, keyswitchable Performance Articulations that replace Poly Articulations

Improved Perfomance view UI

Mic position faders are now controllable via MIDI cc

Improved memory (RAM) handling

Variations can now have an individual MIDI CC per instrument

https://orchestraltools.example/link/aeed438d9f710225

=E2=80=8A

Please note: If you have a saved state from a previous version of the SINEpla=
yer containing a polymap, this will automatically be converted to a Performan=
ce Articulation on first load. However, saved states from 1.4
won't be compatible with previous versions.

You'll find a complete list of features, improvements, and bugfixes in the of=
ficial SINE changelog
https://orchestraltools.example/link/86d05b912ffd9f7b.

As always, this SINEplayer update is completely free of charge.

Update now
https://orchestraltools.example/link/5fc7f16ceda824e3

https://youtube.example/link/32b13c224a9cd18f

